{
	"$schema": "https://schemas.wp.org/trunk/wp-env.json",

	"//": [
		"Copy this file to .wp-env.override.json to run Debloater Pro's",
		"integration tests. The copy is gitignored; this template is not.",
		"",
		"Pro is a separate, private repository. Its integration tests assert",
		"what Pro does to a site running Debloater, so they need both plugins",
		"in one WordPress -- and wp-env can only map a directory that exists.",
		"A mapping like this one in .wp-env.json would therefore break",
		"`wp-env start` for everybody who does not have Pro checked out, which",
		"is everybody but us. Hence a template, and a copy nobody has to have.",
		"",
		"The path is a sibling checkout, which is the layout both repositories'",
		"READMEs describe:",
		"",
		"    Wordpress Plugins/",
		"      debloater/          <- this one",
		"      debloater-pro/",
		"",
		"Change it if yours is somewhere else. Then:",
		"",
		"    npm run env:start",
		"    npm run test:integration:pro",
		"",
		"See debloater-pro/docs/DECISIONS.md D-0065."
	],

	"mappings": {
		"wp-content/plugins/debloater-pro": "../debloater-pro"
	},

	"env": {
		"tests": {
			"mappings": {
				"wp-content/plugins/debloater-pro": "../debloater-pro"
			}
		}
	}
}
